            ('p', 'Bank Rate, often called the base rate, is set by the Bank of England’s Monetary Policy Committee at scheduled meetings through the year. Every decision makes headlines, and business owners reasonably want to know what it means for them. The honest answer is that it depends on the type of borrowing you have, how it is priced and when it was agreed.'),
